>  5. He will escape to the level below.

No. He will do that only if he'd have some additional means, like a
wand of digging. That's not the typical situation.

>  6. Teleport to the down stairs.  Go down.
>  7. If this level also allows teleport, repeat from step 1.
>  (If not, you don't want him fleeing down again,
>   because you can't teleport to those stairs.)
>  8. Step off the up stair (but stay next to it).
>  9. He will come stand on the up stair.
> 10. Whack him once, and he'll escape up.
> 11. Go up.  Now you are on a level that allows teleport.
> 12. Repeat from step 1.
> 
> I usually have to go through this cycle about three times before he
> finally keels over.

Obviously you are doing it wrong.

> It works, but it's annoying to have to tediously lure him up past d5
> non-teleport demon lairs to finally get to a level where you can
> teleport. [...]

The simple procedure is; on the level of his lair lure him one level
down, in case you're not on the upstairs after you descended you will
have to dance a few turns to get there, there you can hit him until
death, since he will not leave your vicinity.

